From: JiaY-shi <shi05275@163.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 16:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: allow API-1 AHB devices in MLO groups

The firmware feature bitmap is carried by the firmware-2.bin API and the
MLO bit was introduced specifically to reject incompatible QCN9274
firmware. IPQ5332 AHB firmware is loaded as split MDT images and therefore
uses firmware API-1 without a feature bitmap.

Do not reject an AHB member of a multi-device WSI group merely because it
has no API-2 feature bitmap. Partner PCI devices continue to require the
MLO firmware feature bit.

Signed-off-by: JiaY-shi <shi05275@163.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
@@ -2233,14 +2233,26 @@ void ath12k_core_hw_group_set_mlo_capabl
 		if (!ab)
 			continue;
 
+		/* AHB firmware is loaded through split MDT images and has no
+		 * firmware-2.bin feature bitmap. The WSI graph describes whether
+		 * the device participates in an inter-device MLO group.
+		 */
+		if (ab->hif.bus == ATH12K_BUS_AHB && !ab->fw.fw_features_valid)
+			continue;
+
 		/* even if 1 device's firmware feature indicates MLO
 		 * unsupported, make MLO unsupported for the whole group
 		 */
 		if (!ath12k_fw_feature_supported(ab, ATH12K_FW_FEATURE_MLO)) {
+			ath12k_info(ab, "WSI group %d: MLO disabled by firmware feature\n",
+				    ag->id);
 			ag->mlo_capable = false;
 			return;
 		}
 	}
+
+	ath12k_info(ag->ab[0], "WSI group %d: MLO enabled for %d devices\n",
+		    ag->id, ag->num_devices);
 }
 
 int ath12k_core_init(struct ath12k_base *ab)
